    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can choose to make the data searchable by other users in the account or you can restrict search access. Searchable data means that all users with access to the OpsItem Overview page (as provided by the DescribeOpsItems API operation) can view and search on the specified data. Operational data that isn’t searchable is only viewable by users who have access to the OpsItem (as provided by the GetOpsItem API operation).",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use the [[p0]] key in OperationalData to specify a related resource in the request. Use the [[p1]] key in OperationalData to associate an Automation runbook with the OpsItem. To view Amazon Web Services CLI example commands that use these keys, see [[p2]] in the [[p3]]Amazon Web Services Systems Manager User Guide[[p4]] .",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
